From: Leopold Li <leopold.lixiaoliang@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 22:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 9] fix(gateway): semantic plist comparison to prevent false refresh cascade

launchd_plist_is_current() was comparing XML text after basic whitespace
normalization. The installed plist (written by plistlib) uses tab-indented
alphabetical key order; the template uses space-indented custom key order.
The text comparison always returned False, causing every hermes gateway
install/start to detect a "stale" plist and call refresh_launchd_plist_if_needed(),
which runs bootout+bootstrap+kickstart → triggering restart cascades.

Fix: parse both plists as Python dicts via plistlib and compare semantically.
PATH value in EnvironmentVariables is still normalized (replaced with sentinel)
to handle cross-shell PATH differences. Falls back to text comparison if
plistlib parsing fails.

diff --git a/hermes_cli/gateway.py b/hermes_cli/gateway.py
--- a/hermes_cli/gateway.py (launchd_plist_is_current, ~line 3978)
+++ b/hermes_cli/gateway.py
Text comparison replaced with plistlib.loads() dict comparison.
